      en: "The Yie substation is a vital component of the Republic of the Congo's national electricity infrastructure, located strategically to distribute power across the southern regions and into the capital, Brazzaville. It serves as a major junction for the energy generated by the Imboulou hydroelectric dam, which is one of the country's most significant power sources. By regulating and stepping down the high-voltage electricity for domestic and industrial use, the facility plays a crucial role in maintaining grid stability and preventing widespread outages in the metropolitan area. The substation has seen various technological upgrades in recent years to support the growing energy demands of the urban population and the expanding industrial sector. Its operation is managed by the national utility company, and it remains a key site for ongoing energy cooperation projects. Beyond its technical function, the Yie substation represents the nation's commitment to modernizing its utilities and providing the necessary energy foundation for long-term economic development and improved living standards.",
      es: "La subestación de Yie es una infraestructura crítica para el suministro eléctrico de Brazzaville y las regiones circundantes. Sirve como un importante centro en la red eléctrica nacional y recibe energía de grandes centrales eléctricas como la presa de Imboulou. La instalación es vital para estabilizar el voltaje y distribuir la electricidad en la capital.",
